As stocks gain momentum, they undergo periods of fast moves followed by pullbacks and consolidation. 

The pullbacks and consolidation periods offer you an opportunity to anticipate a breakout and enter with a very close stop or with an order a few cents above the consolidation.

$NEON
 and $VOXX are good examples of this for today.

What to look for in good anticipation setup
1 series of narrow-range days in pullback/consolidation
2 orderly pullback with no 4% b/d during the pullback or consolidation
3 low-volume pullback
4 low volatility during pullback
5 linear first leg if looking as a continuation setup
The stock should go up smoothly and not in a volatile manner
6  Three to ten days consolidation/pullback
7  not up 3 days in a row
